      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, just overlook the EXIT_FASTPATH_REENTER_GUEST. Currently the vcpu_run() will not return EXIT_FASTPATH_REENTER_GUEST, as below code is the only place to return this but hv_timer_soft_disabled is false when preemption timer happens as the pkvm only use preemption time to trigger immediate exit but not have the case mentioned in the comment.\n```\n          /*\n           * In the *extremely* unlikely scenario that this is a spurious VM-Exit\n           * due to the timer expiring while it was \"soft\" disabled, just eat the\n           * exit and re-enter the guest.\n           */\n          if (unlikely(vmx-\u003eloaded_vmcs-\u003ehv_timer_soft_disabled))\n                  return EXIT_FASTPATH_REENTER_GUEST;\n\n```\nBut if to keep the way as this patch did, then probably need to add more logic to break the for loop if there is any pending request, in case EXIT_FASTPATH_REENTER_GUEST is returned in the future. Anyway, I don\u0027t intend to change this logic in this patch. Will recover it to the original logic. Thanks for caching this.",
